    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the executive law, in relation to authorities and\nresponsibilities during disaster emergencies and in relation to establishing\nthe international emergency management assistance compact",
    "basePrintNo": "S9757",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S9757-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §29-b, add §§29-k & 29-l, Exec L",
    "lawSection": "Executive Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S9757\n\nSPONSOR: SCARCELLA-SPANTON\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the executive law, in relation to authorities and\nresponsibilities during disaster emergencies and in relation to estab-\nlishing the international emergency management assistance compact\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nTo authorize New York State to participate in the Northern Emergency\nManagement Assistance Compact and the International Emergency Management\nAssistance Compact, strengthening interstate and international cooper-\nation in disaster response and emergency management.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends subdivision one of section 29-b of the Executive Law to\nclarify the Governor's authority to deploy certain non-state resource\nproviders during disaster emergencies under interstate emergency assist-\nance compacts.\n\nSections 2 adds a new section 29-k to the Executive Law authorizing the\nGovernor, on behalf of the State, to enter the Northern Emergency\nManagement Assistance Compact and providing that the compact shall be\ndeemed ratified upon certification to the Legislature and the\n\nSecretary of State.\n\nSection 3 adds a new section 29-1 to the Executive Law authorizing the\nGovernor, on behalf of the State, to enter the International Emergency\nManagement Assistance Compact, and providing that the compact shall\nlikewise be deemed ratified upon certification to the Legislature and\nthe Secretary of State.\n\nSection 4 establishes the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nDisasters frequently require coordinated responses across state and\ninternational borders. Participation in formal emergency management\ncompacts allows jurisdictions to share resources, personnel, and exper-\ntise during emergencies while ensuring clear operational procedures and\nlegal protections for responding entities.  This bill authorizes New\nYork State to participate in two established mutual aid agreements: the\nNorthern Emergency Management Assistance Compact and the International\nEmergency Management Assistance Compact. These compacts facilitate coor-\ndinated disaster response between neigh- boring states and Canadian\nprovinces and strengthen regional prepared- ness for natural disasters,\npublic health emergencies, and other large- scale incidents. By enabling\nparticipation in these compacts, the legislation enhances New York's\nability to respond to emergencies and collaborate with regional partners\nduring times of crisis.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
